From: Yury Klushin <digger@live.ru>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 23:09:05 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] pdp11: save the frame pointer when a frame is needed

pdp11_saved_regno asked the dataflow whether a register had ever been
live, which is the right question for a call-saved register in general
and the wrong one for the frame pointer.  LRA can decide that a frame
is needed after the dataflow has stopped looking -- an asm that
clobbers the stack pointer is enough -- and nothing goes back to mark
r5 live.  The prologue then builds its frame in r5 without saving it,
and the epilogue returns without putting it back:

  _f:   mov  sp,r5          _f:   mov  r5,-(sp)
        add  $-010,sp             mov  sp,r5
        ...            ->         add  $-010,sp
        mov  r5,sp                ...
        rts  pc                   mov  r5,sp
                                  mov  (sp)+,r5
                                  rts  pc

r5 is call-saved here, so a caller holding anything in it simply lost
it across the call.  Only under -mlra; the old allocator marks the
register live in time.

From prcoder-1/digger-bk0010's GCC patch for the BK-0010, where it was
found; the test is this tree's.
---
 gcc/config/pdp11/pdp11.cc                     | 11 +++++++-
 .../gcc.target/pdp11/lra-frame-pointer.c      | 25 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 35 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
 create mode 100644 gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/pdp11/lra-frame-pointer.c

diff --git a/gcc/config/pdp11/pdp11.cc b/gcc/config/pdp11/pdp11.cc
index 017f601..488731b 100644
--- a/gcc/config/pdp11/pdp11.cc
+++ b/gcc/config/pdp11/pdp11.cc
@@ -332,7 +332,16 @@ static bool pdp11_scalar_mode_supported_p (scalar_mode);
 static inline bool
 pdp11_saved_regno (unsigned regno)
 {
-  return !call_used_or_fixed_reg_p (regno) && df_regs_ever_live_p (regno);
+  /* The frame pointer has to be saved whenever a frame pointer is
+     needed, and asking the dataflow whether it was ever live is not
+     the same question: LRA can decide late that a frame is needed --
+     an asm that clobbers the stack pointer is enough -- and nothing
+     goes back to mark the register live.  The prologue then builds a
+     frame in a call-saved register it never saved, and the epilogue
+     returns without putting it back.  */
+  return !call_used_or_fixed_reg_p (regno)
+	 && (df_regs_ever_live_p (regno)
+	     || (regno == HARD_FRAME_POINTER_REGNUM && frame_pointer_needed));
 }
 
 /* Expand the function prologue.  */
diff --git a/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/pdp11/lra-frame-pointer.c b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/pdp11/lra-frame-pointer.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5cbe334
--- /dev/null
+++ b/gcc/testsuite/gcc.target/pdp11/lra-frame-pointer.c
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+/* { dg-do compile { target pdp11-*-* } } */
+/* { dg-options "-O2 -mlra" } */
+
+/* An asm that clobbers the stack pointer makes a frame pointer
+   necessary, and under LRA that decision comes after the dataflow has
+   stopped looking -- so r5 was never marked live, the prologue built a
+   frame in it without saving it, and the epilogue returned without
+   putting it back.  r5 is call-saved here, so the caller simply lost
+   it.  */
+
+extern void g (int *);
+
+int
+f (int n)
+{
+  int a[4];
+
+  g (a);
+  asm volatile ("" ::: "sp");
+  return a[n & 3];
+}
+
+/* Saved on the way in and restored on the way out.  */
+/* { dg-final { scan-assembler "mov\tr5,-\\(sp\\)" } } */
+/* { dg-final { scan-assembler "mov\t\\(sp\\)\\+,r5" } } */
